1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Going to the Cinema

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:20,520
I like to go to the cinema to see films. My favourite films have action, comedy, and cars that can talk.

3
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:27,720
I will never, ever watch a musical. If it has dancing and singing, I know I will cry.

4
00:00:39,720 --> 00:00:50,800
For a long time, Kuan has been afraid to see films. He would just close his eyes and bury his head into Dad's chest whenever anything scary appeared on thescreen.

5
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:56,800
He's braver now and only covers his eyes a little.

6
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:09,880
The cinema has lots of video games, bright lights, and a huge place to buy candies and snacks

7
00:01:21,880 --> 00:01:29,290
I think the food is my favourite part of going to the cinema.There's popcorn, chips, and sugaron everything.

8
00:01:29,290 --> 00:01:35,670
"Who should buy popcorn?" I say, interested to see if Dad gets the hint.

9
00:01:41,670 --> 00:01:49,200
"Kuan can buy it," he says, smiling. Kuan and I have saved some money this week for a new toy.

10
00:01:55,200 --> 00:02:03,670
Still, snacks would be nice. Kuan and I decide to use our money and buy some snacks before the film begins.

11
00:02:09,670 --> 00:02:16,100
We bring our snacks to the cinema, the crowd gets quiet, and the film comes onthe screen.

12
00:02:28,100 --> 00:02:37,620
Ialwaysget a littlenervousbefore thefilm starts. Ihope it's interesting. Iat leasthopeI won'tbebored!

13
00:02:37,620 --> 00:02:46,760
This film has cars that talk, my favourite actor, and a car thatknowskarate.In otherwords, it has all of theparts of a great film.

14
00:02:58,760 --> 00:03:08,140
Kuan and I arelaughing out loud! We have got to see it again. We'll be talking about the film at thedinner tablefor aweek.

15
00:03:08,140 --> 00:03:14,140
Dad will not be. He's snoring.
